        "tagline": "FAQ",
        "title": "Asked before signing up",
        "items": [
          {
            "title": "Is the free plan a trial?",
            "description": "No. One project, unlimited notes, forever, with a small Cadence badge in the footer. We would rather you outgrow it than have it expire on you."
          },
          {
            "title": "What happens to my notes if we leave?",
            "description": "Export to Markdown with the images, one click, no support ticket. The public page can also be handed over as static files you host yourself."
          },
          {
            "title": "Does the AI write the final text?",
            "description": "It writes the draft; a person publishes. Nothing reaches your customers without a human pressing publish, and the diff between draft and published is kept so you can see what it got wrong."
          },
          {
            "title": "Where is our data?",
            "description": "Frankfurt, on the hosted plan. SOC 2 Type II report on request, subprocessors listed publicly, and the self-hosted plan exists precisely for teams who cannot accept any of that."
          },
          {
            "title": "We ship once a quarter. Is this for us?",
            "description": "Honestly, probably not. Below about one release a month, a page in your wiki does the job. Come back when the wiki page starts going stale."
          }
        ]
